Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 15 at 4:08PM MDT until August 15 at 7:15PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"FFWBOU\n\nThe National Weather Service in Denver has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNortheastern Weld County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* Until 715 PM MDT.\n\n* At 408 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1.5 to 3 inches in 1\nhour. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 1.5 inches are possible\nin the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, gulches,\nroads, and poor drainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Northeastern Weld County.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nSpring Creek, Twomile Creek, Horsetail Creek, Cottonwood Creek,\nSidney Draw, George Creek and North Pawnee Creek.","ends":"2026-08-15T19:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce6c93571f18dc9a010aab6730c960783abe9c78.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce6c93571f18dc9a010aab6730c960783abe9c78.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 15 at 3:16PM MDT until August 15 at 6:15PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\nCentral Weld County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 615 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 316 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms over northern Weld County, moving slowly east.\nMinor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly in the\nadvisory area. Up to 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nKeota, Briggsdale, Jackson Reservoir, New Raymer, Purcell,\nBuckingham and Cornish.","ends":"2026-08-15T18:15:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Morgan, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1040d9f13a0ef590283f4685e4ca77bfd38c4bd4.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.1040d9f13a0ef590283f4685e4ca77bfd38c4bd4.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 2:05PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n584 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 9 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              DOUGLAS\nLOGAN                 MORGAN                WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, AURORA, CASTLE ROCK,\nCENTENNIAL, ELIZABETH, FORT MORGAN, GREELEY, KIOWA, LIMON,\nPARKER, STERLING, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Lincoln, CO; Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:52AM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central and northeast Colorado, including the\nfollowing areas: the southern Front Range Foothills, Palmer Divide\narea, I-25 corridor, and all of our eastern plains counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional thunderstorms and heavy rainfall this afternoon,\ncombined with the heavy rainfall from the past 3 days, will bring\na threat for flash flooding this afternoon and evening. Stronger\nstorms will be capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30\nminutes, with isolated areas receiving storm totals of 2 to 4\ninches.","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Northeast Weld County; Central and South Weld County; Morgan County; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties; North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-15T19:12:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 151912 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 112 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Another round of showers and thunderstorms this afternoon and evening. Heavy rainfall and flash flooding are the main threats today. A few thunderstorms could